 "content": "# Translated motif copies\n\nFor a noisy grid with a distinctive single-color motif amid zeros and another background color, record the motif-colored cell offsets from its bounding box. Search for in-bounds translations whose corresponding cells are all zero, and recolor only those matching positions with the motif color. Preserve all other cells, including the original motif and zeros or background-colored cells inside its bounding box. Do not infer flood-fill or neighbor propagation from appearance alone. A small script can enumerate translations; allow rotation or reflection only when demonstrations support it. Check candidate changes against the demonstrations.\n"
}

