 "path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-openclaw-luna6-high-ws0/frozen/held-out-3/play/users/u031/system/state/openclaw/agents/main/agent/workshop-skills/continual-arc/diagonal-periodic-fill.md",
 "content": "# Periodic diagonal fill\n\nFor sparse colored diagonal markers on a zero field, identify the invariant of their parallel lines: row−column for down-right diagonals, or row+column for down-left diagonals. Demonstrations may indicate that the output fills the whole grid with a periodic color sequence indexed by that invariant. With zero-based coordinates, use column−row for the down-right phase and row+column for down-left. Infer the smallest plausible period that does not assign conflicting colors to the same residue, and use demonstrated outputs to establish the full phase-to-color mapping when available. Marker positions alone may not determine every residue. Color every cell from the supported phase mapping and check it against demonstrated outputs.\n"
}

